WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:01.260
Congratulations!

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:06.729
You’ve just started your new job at the
SCP Foundation as a Junior Researcher.

00:00:06.729 --> 00:00:11.060
We hope you survive long enough to retire
and collect your Foundation pension - but

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:14.570
you’ve got a lot to learn before you can
even think about that.

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:18.760
You’re here to find out more about some
of the most mysterious entities known to man,

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:24.440
and the Foundation depends on you to do your
job right, or the world might not see tomorrow

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:26.070
- but hey, no pressure.

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:29.180
You’re gonna hear a lot of new terminology
on the job.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:32.610
Big, scary words like “Apollyon” and “Thaumatology.”

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:38.670
And, of course, “Euclid” and “Keter”,
the two most common containment classifications.

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:43.329
Today, we’re gonna answer a question that’s
been on a lot of people’s minds: What do

00:00:43.329 --> 00:00:48.010
these classifications actually mean, and what’s
the difference between them?

00:00:48.010 --> 00:00:52.219
First, it must be noted that these classes
don’t have as much to do with danger as

00:00:52.219 --> 00:00:53.600
you may think.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:58.879
Instead, object classes are all about how
difficult an anomaly is to contain.

00:00:58.879 --> 00:01:03.059
And we’re going to take you on a crash course
of each of them, and provide some examples

00:01:03.059 --> 00:01:07.230
so you can broaden your idea of what exactly
“Euclid”, “Keter”, and all the other

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:09.620
classes of anomalies can be.

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:14.210
Of course, while Euclid and Keter are perhaps
the best known object classes, they aren’t

00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:15.540
the only ones.

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:19.100
Just below them, in terms of severity, is
the “Safe” Class.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:24.300
It may be every guard and D-Class’s dream
to get assigned to “Safe” SCPs, but this

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:28.450
classification doesn’t mean that the anomaly
in question is harmless.

00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:33.350
It does mean that they are easy to contain
though, often requiring very few resources

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:36.600
or certain specific activation mechanisms.

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:44.500
For example, SCP-507, the unwilling dimension
hopper, is fully cooperative with Foundation

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:48.500
containment protocols, earning him the “Safe”
class.

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:54.170
SCP-662, the Butler’s Hand Bell, while capable
of extreme violence, doesn’t activate unless

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:57.710
someone rings it, making it “safe” to
store.

00:01:57.710 --> 00:02:03.140
And of course, SCP-999, the Tickle Monster,
earned its “Safe” rating by essentially

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:08.200
wanting to keep Foundation staff pleased at
every turn and requiring virtually nothing

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:10.499
in the way of containment.

00:02:10.499 --> 00:02:12.099
Euclid comes next.

00:02:12.099 --> 00:02:16.980
This class actually has the widest scope of
any object class under Foundation control,

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:19.980
and the grand majority of objects fall under
this banner.

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:25.389
Unlike Safe class anomalies, Euclid anomalies
require greater resources to keep contained.

00:02:25.389 --> 00:02:30.280
The “Euclid” Classification can also mean
that containment isn’t always reliable,

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:34.499
and is often given due to either a lack of
knowledge about the anomaly or there being

00:02:34.499 --> 00:02:37.269
some degree of inherent unpredictability.

00:02:37.269 --> 00:02:42.860
“Unpredictable” is really the key word
when it comes to Euclid SCPs.

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:46.840
Anomalies that are either autonomous, meaning
they can move on their own; sentient, meaning

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:51.260
that they are capable of thought; or Sapient,
meaning they are particularly intelligent,

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:55.040
almost always automatically fall into the
Euclid Class.

00:02:55.040 --> 00:03:00.519
This is because anything that moves or thinks
on its own is capable of surprising and unpredictable

00:03:00.519 --> 00:03:01.560
behavior.

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:05.769
Notwithstanding certain exceptions like the
aforementioned Tickle Monster.

00:03:05.769 --> 00:03:07.650
This brings us to Keter.

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:12.510
In the simplest terms, you could describe
Keter class anomalies as “Euclid but worse.”

00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:18.519
Again, this has nothing to do with how violent
or dangerous the anomaly is, merely how difficult

00:03:18.519 --> 00:03:20.400
it is to contain.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:25.800
Keter Class anomalies often require extensive
resources to fully contain.

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:30.849
Containment methods are also often extra thorough
and complex, though when it comes to a Keter

00:03:30.849 --> 00:03:36.669
Class anomaly, there’s no guarantee the
methods will be one hundred percent effective.

00:03:36.669 --> 00:03:42.129
There are a number of reasons an SCP can slip
into Keter territory including, but not limited

00:03:42.129 --> 00:03:47.389
to, extreme aggression in its frequent escape
attempts, existing in large numbers over a

00:03:47.389 --> 00:03:53.040
wide area, and having anomalous abilities
that make them particularly difficult to contain,

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:56.519
like teleportation or the ability to walk
through walls.

00:03:56.519 --> 00:04:01.129
To better explain this, Foundation researchers
have devised a simple method known as the

00:04:01.129 --> 00:04:02.510
“Locked Box Test.”

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:06.709
If you were to leave an item inside a locked
box and stop supervising it, and it’s still

00:04:06.709 --> 00:04:10.340
there when you get back, then that item is
probably “Safe.”

00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:14.760
If you leave an item inside a locked box without
supervision and you’re not sure what exactly

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:17.560
will happen, then it’s probably “Euclid.”

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:22.290
If you leave an item inside a locked box without
supervision and it easily breaks free, then

00:04:22.290 --> 00:04:25.240
you likely have a “Keter” object on your
hands.

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:28.980
Or rather, did, before it broke out and ran
off.

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:32.980
Before we go any further, it’s worth briefly
mentioning that there are two other primary

00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:38.350
object classes that cover most SCPs that aren’t
under the “Safe”, “Euclid”, and “Keter”

00:04:38.350 --> 00:04:39.350
banners.

00:04:39.350 --> 00:04:41.290
These are “Thaumiel” and “Neutralized.”

00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:48.130
Thaumiel anomalies are SCPs that are used
to contain other SCPs - such as SCP-3000,

00:04:48.130 --> 00:04:51.440
the legendary Amnestic-producing Anantashesha.

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:55.510
Neutralized anomalies are objects that have
either lost their anomalous qualities or been

00:04:55.510 --> 00:04:56.830
straight-up destroyed.

00:04:56.830 --> 00:05:04.840
A good example being SCP-1762, the cardboard
box which used to contain the land of Fantasy.

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:09.250
But back to Euclid and Keter: What are some
good examples of Euclid and Keter class anomalies

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:10.970
in containment right now?

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:15.900
Let’s take a look at some of the Foundation’s
most iconic Euclid-classes first.

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:21.620
Kicking things off, we have SCP-096, also
known as the Shy Guy.

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:25.980
We all know and fear this self-conscious,
serial-killing monster that murders anything

00:05:25.980 --> 00:05:27.870
that sees its face.

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:32.190
As you already know, when someone sees the
face of the Shy Guy, nothing can stand in

00:05:32.190 --> 00:05:35.240
its way on its quest to utterly destroy them.

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:39.830
The monster has not only proven successful
in causing mass casualty events, it’s also

00:05:39.830 --> 00:05:44.340
pretty much indestructible and has shown that
it’s able to tear its way out of containment

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:45.340
with ease.

00:05:45.340 --> 00:05:49.400
So, you may be wondering, why is the Shy Guy
Euclid and not Keter?

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:55.770
While it may surprise you to hear this, SCP-096
is actually closer to “Safe” than “Keter.”

00:05:55.770 --> 00:06:00.070
The monster may be incredibly dangerous when
its rage state is activated, but it’s proven

00:06:00.070 --> 00:06:03.910
fairly easy for the Foundation to control
this activation.

00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:08.570
The only times that 096 has breached containment
is when photographs of its face have been

00:06:08.570 --> 00:06:13.390
found out in the world, but as long as the
Foundation can prevent people from seeing

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:17.480
its face, it poses no real risk of containment
breach.

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:21.560
The very fact that the Foundation can’t
know for sure how many photos of it are out

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:26.930
there adds an element of unpredictability
to its containment, and that is why - despite

00:06:26.930 --> 00:06:32.580
being incredibly scary and dangerous - 096
is firmly Euclid.

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:41.190
Next, another Euclid anomaly that needs no
introduction: SCP-173, also known as The Sculpture.

00:06:41.190 --> 00:06:46.120
This nasty piece of modern art has given workers
at the Foundation many a sleepless night thanks

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:51.240
to its terrifying tendency to snap the necks
of anyone who isn’t looking at it.

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:57.590
This is a creature so scary that even SCP-682
feels uncomfortable around it.

00:06:57.590 --> 00:07:04.760
Much like SCP-096, 173 has also proved nigh
impossible to kill, and in a containment breach,

00:07:04.760 --> 00:07:08.230
it’s been known to stack up bodies like
it was judgment day.

00:07:08.230 --> 00:07:11.070
So, why just Euclid rather than Keter?

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:16.720
Once again, it all comes down to the Foundation
understanding just how 173 ticks.

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:21.830
As everyone knows by now, 173 is paralyzed
whenever someone is looking at it.

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:25.800
As a result, the Foundation has been able
to devise containment methods that center

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:29.380
around keeping 173 constantly observed.

00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:34.260
The reason it’s Euclid rather than safe
is that, while quite reliable, this method

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:37.170
is also somewhat time and resource intensive.

00:07:37.170 --> 00:07:41.840
And as with anything that requires a high
degree of human involvement, the potential

00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:44.690
for human error is always there.

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:51.400
And finally, in our rundown of famous Euclid
class objects, we have SCP-3008, more broadly

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:54.400
known as the infinite Ikea.

00:07:54.400 --> 00:07:59.450
This sinister retail giant is a pocket dimension
hiding within an Ikea superstore, leading

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:04.680
to what seems to be an infinite furniture
warehouse, filled with scary, faceless creatures

00:08:04.680 --> 00:08:06.840
known as The Staff.

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:11.651
Hundreds or perhaps even thousands of people
have become trapped in SCP-3008, and it may

00:08:11.651 --> 00:08:14.440
even connect to other dimensions.

00:08:14.440 --> 00:08:18.400
This is one place where you really, really
don’t want to get stuck while shopping for

00:08:18.400 --> 00:08:20.540
a new piece of furniture.

00:08:20.540 --> 00:08:22.200
But it’s still Euclid.

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:23.200
Why?

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:27.820
Well, because - to the best of our knowledge
- there’s only one gateway into 3008’s

00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:34.280
pocket dimension inside our reality, and the
Foundation has that specific site on lockdown.

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:39.080
While there are still things we don’t know
about SCP-3008, the Foundation has been able

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:41.450
to secure and contain the entrance.

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:45.529
It’s Euclid rather than “Safe” because
this entrance still needs to be patrolled

00:08:45.529 --> 00:08:50.650
regularly to ward off any Staff attempting
to escape, and prevent further victims from

00:08:50.650 --> 00:08:54.950
entering, which is a low risk but resource-heavy
job.

00:08:54.950 --> 00:08:56.460
Next up is Keter Class.

00:08:56.460 --> 00:09:02.890
First, we have the terrifying SCP-682, also
known as the Hard to Destroy Reptile.

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:07.020
Anyone who’s seen our videos on this nasty
creature knows that it really, really lives

00:09:07.020 --> 00:09:08.400
up to that name.

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:14.050
682 may not be the most dangerous SCP - especially
with cosmic monsters like the Scarlet King

00:09:14.050 --> 00:09:18.330
and the Devourer of Worlds out there - but
it’s one of the most hardy, thanks to its

00:09:18.330 --> 00:09:21.280
incredible adaptive abilities.

00:09:21.280 --> 00:09:25.920
Because of the way 682 adapts to pretty much
any threat, it’s virtually impossible to

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:28.200
attack it the same way twice.

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:33.450
However, if being violent and indestructible
was all it took to become a Keter class anomaly,

00:09:33.450 --> 00:09:35.730
the Shy Guy would be right there with it.

00:09:35.730 --> 00:09:41.130
There are two key factors that push 682 into
Keter territory: Its incredibly high intelligence

00:09:41.130 --> 00:09:46.150
and the fact it reacts unpredictably to all
external stimuli.

00:09:46.150 --> 00:09:51.750
Because of its intelligence, 682 is able to
actively scheme to escape containment, something

00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:57.080
it does with such regularity that the Foundation
is constantly trying to terminate it.

00:09:57.080 --> 00:10:01.670
And because of its adaptive abilities, its
behavior in response to containment is often

00:10:01.670 --> 00:10:04.070
nigh impossible to predict.

00:10:04.070 --> 00:10:10.360
As a result of all this, 682 is a complete
nightmare to keep locked up, making it Keter.

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:16.830
Next, a Keter Class anomaly that’s not quite
as well known and not nearly as ferocious:

00:10:16.830 --> 00:10:22.200
SCP-3663, also known as The Tunnel Monster
or the Cardboard Box Monster.

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:27.760
This entity is as scary as it is incredibly
sad - he was once a normal little boy, playing

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:30.820
in an abandoned industrial area with his friends.

00:10:30.820 --> 00:10:35.660
He had built himself a crude monster costume
out of cardboard boxes, but through anomalous

00:10:35.660 --> 00:10:41.200
means, this costume bonded with the little
boy, turning his organs into cardboard and

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:42.200
twine.

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:46.750
Now, it manifests in pipes and tunnels across
the country, approaching nearby humans and

00:10:46.750 --> 00:10:48.810
causing paranoia and fear.

00:10:48.810 --> 00:10:52.650
It’ll then grab his victims, and transport
them elsewhere.

00:10:52.650 --> 00:10:56.140
Leaving them unconscious and afraid, but otherwise
unharmed.

00:10:56.140 --> 00:11:00.779
Clearly, we’re not looking at an anomaly
even close to being as dangerous and deadly

00:11:00.779 --> 00:11:05.260
to SCP-682, but it’s still very much Keter.

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:06.260
Why?

00:11:06.260 --> 00:11:11.050
Because the teleporting ability inherent to
SCP-3663 makes it incredibly difficult to

00:11:11.050 --> 00:11:16.440
consistently contain, along with its inherent
distrust of Foundation personnel.

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:21.450
The Foundation have yet to devise a truly
effective containment method for 3663 and

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:27.960
its teleporting antics, so Keter class is
where it remains, despite being mostly benign.

00:11:27.960 --> 00:11:33.110
And finally, SCP-1000, aka Bigfoot.

00:11:33.110 --> 00:11:38.390
This is one of the few anomalies that genuinely
holds the moral high ground over the Foundation,

00:11:38.390 --> 00:11:43.320
on account of them formerly being an incredibly
advanced species almost wiped out by humanity

00:11:43.320 --> 00:11:44.320
in the past.

00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:48.690
Now, the Foundation is feeding everyone the
lie that even looking at one of these creatures

00:11:48.690 --> 00:11:52.060
can result in death - even though it can’t.

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:57.390
The reality is that the Foundation hopes to
keep SCP-1000 suppressed, fearing that if

00:11:57.390 --> 00:12:02.490
they ever regained their former glory, they
would surely oppress humanity just as humanity

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:04.060
had oppressed them.

00:12:04.060 --> 00:12:10.560
Even though, once again, it doesn’t appear
that SCP-1000 has any such malicious intentions.

00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:15.690
So why are these abnormally large and abnormally
intelligent apes Keter Class?

00:12:15.690 --> 00:12:20.751
Once again, it all comes down to two facts
tipping the classification scales, and in

00:12:20.751 --> 00:12:24.330
this case those are population and dispersion.

00:12:24.330 --> 00:12:28.750
There are a lot of these creatures out there,
especially across North America, and the fact

00:12:28.750 --> 00:12:33.780
they appear in forests all across the country
makes it incredibly difficult for the Foundation

00:12:33.780 --> 00:12:35.440
to keep a lid on them.

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:41.580
Seeing as a civilian simply seeing an SCP-1000
specimen constitutes a containment breach,

00:12:41.580 --> 00:12:46.250
these happen frequently, especially if you
run in cryptid and conspiracy circles and

00:12:46.250 --> 00:12:49.080
are out actually looking to meet one.

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:53.870
That brings us to the end of our crash course
on Euclid and Keter class anomalies.

00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:58.960
We hope you’ve enjoyed your stay, and managed
to survive all the strange and horrific entities

00:12:58.960 --> 00:12:59.960
we’ve covered.

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:03.690
Let us know if you enjoyed this video in the
comments and want to see more of the ins and

00:13:03.690 --> 00:13:07.760
outs of the SCP Foundation’s classification
system explained.

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:12.529
But for now you’re finally ready to start
your research role at the SCP Foundation - just

00:13:12.529 --> 00:13:16.540
make sure you’ve got your last will and
testament written before your first day.

00:13:16.540 --> 00:13:23.480
Now check out “SCP Chaos Insurgency Explained”
and “SCP - 001 - Which Is The Real 001?”

00:13:23.480 --> 00:13:26.490
for more of the SCP Foundation’s most top
secret files!

